WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.500
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for my Arrow bonus video I wanted to talk

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.500
about Malcolm Merlyn.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.050
John Barrowman has been talking a lot about
how the character is different in Season 3

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.309
so I’ll explain what that all means and
count down some of my all time favorite Merlyn

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:15.309
Moments.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:20.500
The real big reminder is that The Flash is
coming Tuesday October 7th and Arrow Wednesday

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.730
October 8th, I’ll be doing videos for all
the episodes.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.730
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:32.879
If you haven’t seen it, Andrew Kriesberg
who’s an executive producer on Arrow and

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:36.059
The Flash did this featurette where he talks
about the themes of Season 3.

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:39.699
You have to pre-order season 3 on iTunes in
order to get the clip.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:40.969
I can’t upload it to youtube.

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:45.019
I saw someone tried and they got the ban hammer
from warner brothers.

00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:52.140
He explains that from Oliver’s perspective
in season 2 it was “am I a killer” and

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.440
in season 3 it’s going to be Identity, “who
am I”.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.249
And that’s going to trickle down to all
the other characters, including Malcolm Merlyn.

00:00:59.249 --> 00:01:04.850
Merlyn and Thea find themselves in this interesting
situation where one has lost his child, Tommy

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.880
and one lost her mother, Moira.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.299
So you have these two try to figure out how
to form a new family unit with Merlyn’s

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:15.799
past and the league of assassin’s casting
this giant shadow over everything they do.

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:16.899
That’s where the fun starts.

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:25.869
Both Oliver and Merlyn have bottled up a lot
of their demons 

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:33.289
and as Kriesberg said, there’s always the
opportunity for those demons to get out.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:39.490
That’s a very eloquent way of saying Ra’s
Al Ghul, the head of the demon, is also Merlyn’s

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.490
Demon.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.450
As well as a demon for everyone.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:49.560
But during the featurette Kreisberg also referenced
Slade in the Argus prison when he talked about

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.490
bottled demons getting out.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:57.460
I’m not expecting Slade to get out, but
they’ve only shot about half of the episodes

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.460
this season.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.299
They haven’t finished writing everything
yet either, so there’s always the opportunity

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:03.850
to bring Manu Bennett back.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.939
The side tangent to the really obvious demons
is Komodo.

00:02:05.939 --> 00:02:07.670
We saw him in the season 3 trailer.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.729
He shows up in episode 2.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.380
In the comics he was linked to Oliver’s
father, but since the show changes a lot of

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.710
things they might link his backstory to both
Oliver and Merlyn.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:19.992
At some point Team Merlyn and Team Arrow have
to collide, probably going to be some League

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:21.530
of Assassin’s Ra’s Al Ghul whatnot.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.940
John Barrowman said that Merlyn is a man ultimately
looking for redemption.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:30.260
And using power to get what he wants ended
in horrible failure, so this season he’s

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.500
taking a more personal approach, playing on
emotions.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:46.050
But all the things he does in season 3 will
be part of that bigger personal 

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.950
mission of redemption.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:03:01.540
I think it’s a really awesome way to think
about the character, it explains why Merlyn

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.690
doesn’t think of himself as a villain.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:12.050
And even though he’s a villain in the comics,
they’ve been able to blur the lines on Arrow.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:17.350
So you should expect a lot of fun awkward
Merlyn Family Moments with Thea.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:21.630
I also wonder what his relationship with Oliver
will be like.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:41.160
Based on the scenes in the trailer it’s
hard to tell when he and Thea come back to

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.890
Starling.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:49.140
It seems like they left town and have been
training somewhere far away.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:53.880
Generally, we’re going to see more of Merlyn
in his own domain, not being crazy sinister

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.950
like in season 1.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:00.900
Here’s my top 5 Malcolm Merlyn Moments from
seasons 1 and 2.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.600
5 - Merlyn Tells Oliver The Hood Should Change
his name to Green Arrow

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.530
This was episode 9 years end from season 1.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.710
Merlyn had just killed Adam Hunt so the Dark
Archer was rearing his head and Oliver was

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.729
still trying to deflect attention from The
Vigilante.

00:04:17.729 --> 00:04:20.570
This was all before people started calling
him the Arrow.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.760
Merlyn had already suspected Oliver might
be the Vigilante, so they’re all at the

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.680
dinner table having a very Hannibal type meal.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:30.960
Maybe we’ll actually get more of those moments
in season 3.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.230
That would be awesome.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.170
Later in that episode too, Merlyn hands Oliver’s
ass to him.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.190
That was one of their first big fights.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.040
The whole thing is just a big wink at the
comics and I loved that they gave the line

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.650
to the big villain of that year.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:49.560
How great is it that the villain can see into
his future in a way Oliver can’t.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.650
At the time he had no idea what Team Arrow
was going to become.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.540
And he’s just now starting to get into Justice
League mode.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.750
That time when he starts teaming up with bigger
and bigger superheros like The Flash.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.532
4 - Merlyn Throws Down In Front Of Tommy For
The First Time

00:05:01.532 --> 00:05:03.340
Wearing a Tuxedo none the less.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.370
This was Season 1 Episode 16 Dead to Rights.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.790
It was fun to see him get his james bond moment.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:13.190
And it got even crazier because Deadshot was
the one trying to kill him.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:18.350
Oliver ended up saving his life and that also
became the moment Tommy learned Oliver was

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.350
the vigilante.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:24.250
3 - Malcolm Merlyn Reveals Himself as the
Dark Archer for the first time

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.550
This was also from the same mid season finale
in season 1.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:31.130
It wasn’t a big surprise for comic book
readers, but the way they filmed it with John

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:38.410
Barrowman throwing his hood back and showing
his face for the first time was epic.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:47.160
2 - Malcolm Merlyn Returns for the First Time
In Season 2

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.980
This was from Season 2 Episode 7, the state
versus moira queen.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.660
Merlyn had fixed the trial to get Moira off
the hook.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.130
And he was just beginning to set his Thea
plot into motion.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.639
He was still very much a Season 1 Merlyn.

00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:05.270
By the time he came back in the season 2 finale
he was much closer to the Merlyn we’ll see

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.270
in season 3.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.610
Less machiavellian but still very dark.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:13.441
1 - Oliver Versus Merlyn in the Season 1 Finale

00:06:13.441 --> 00:06:19.000
Their final battle was one of the best action
sequences all year long and the fight didn’t

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.910
really end.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:25.060
I’m expecting them to pick things back up
where they left off.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:30.210
At least at first, I think they’ll put their
hatred aside and deal with the bigger threat

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.210
together.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:37.060
I was kind of hoping they’d team up against
slade in season 2, but they might have just

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:48.010
been holding that off till season 3.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:52.790
Let me know what your favorite Merlyn moment
is and do you want to see him team up with

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.040
Oliver against Ra’s Al Ghul this season?

